<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n9743" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντευ-πάσχω</span></b>  and <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντευ-ποιέω</span></b>  are by recent edd. written divisim
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντ᾽ εὖ π.</span> (v. <i><span class="en">
			Pl.
			<u>Grg.</u>
			520e
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			X.
			<u>An.</u>
			5.5.21
		</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
			D.
			20.124
		</span></i>), on the ground that <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ</span> never
		enters into direct composition with Verbs, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὖ</span>
			 fin.; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντευποιεῖν</span> is
			read in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>EN</u>
				1179a28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Rh.</u>
				1374a24
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
